This repository contains the training, data preparation, export and evaluation
code of the Luciole Audio models, speech and audio augmented language models
(SALM) built on the Luciole models, developed by LINAGORA within the
OpenLLM-France consortium.
PROJET FRANCE2030 OpenLLM-France, funded by Bpifrance under the call
"Communs numériques pour l'intelligence artificielle générative".

The Luciole Audio models (Luciole-1B-Audio-1.0, Luciole-8B-Audio-1.0 and
Luciole-23B-Audio-1.0) are the property of LINAGORA SAS and are released under
the Apache License 2.0.
The Luciole-Audio-Training-Dataset and Luciole-Audio-Evaluation-Dataset are
collections curated by LINAGORA SAS: the curation layer and each collection as a
whole are released under CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0, while every source dataset remains
under its own licence (see the dataset cards).

